Considering I already had some daggers and the 100 or so I found all
stacked with mine once I threw them on the altar, no real luck there.
+0 daggers are still decent throwing weapons, but they are pretty much
anywhere.
Luckily, I found a wand of cancellation amongst the bones, so I had an
easy time fixing the most of the cursed items and generating some
water for blessing from potions i'd rather not use.  One of the bags
had a potion of holy water as well, so off to a good start, I figure.
I end up blessing+using the 3 lamps I found and wish for the
obligatory GDSM first and boots of speed second.  Third, I go for an
amulet of life saving, since my amulet spot is still open and since I
tend to be horribly reckless.  Now that I think back on it, gauntlets
of strength probably would have been more useful since I haven't died
yet.  I still have my own personal magic lamp in case I need something
other than a permanent light source though.

I would have wished for magicbane, but I thought it was too risky
since I tend to switch weapons alot and might get blasted to death,
and also since there were already 2 artifacts.

After all that, my AC was about -14, so I figured I was safe for mines
end.  All in all, things went pretty well, except that I lost half a
level to vampire lords due to recklessness.  Also, for some reason I
found a trap door that sent me down even lower(a bug?).

Now I'm past my quest level and am clearing the dungeon for xp.  Only
one problem: even after exhausting 3 wands of create monster and a bag
of tricks, I still am wielding a +2 runed dagger, which is my only
viable weapon against rust monsters, and the rest of my daggers are
+0.

Next chapter: The one where I probably run into a Gelatinous cube and
proceed to lose any remaining enchantments I have to disenchanters,
followed by an encounter with a mind flayer where my wand of digging
runs out of charges at a crucial moment, I accidentally read a scroll
of destroy armor due to stupidity, and the subsequent sacrificing of a
cockatrice without gloves on!

Okay, that is if my luck stays good that all of that will happen.
Stay tuned, folks!



